BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kong Mexico City|Intelligent Model Routing\, Governed: NVIDIA NeMo
  Switchyard + Kong AI Gateway|Online
DTSTART:20261105T100000
CATEGORIES:ai,data,security
DESCRIPTION:Kong/MEXICO-CITY\nNot every step in an AI agent workflow needs
  the most powerful and expensive model. So can you ensure every request re
 aches the right model without sacrificing performance\, security\, or cont
 rol?\nAs enterprises move toward multi-model agentic AI\, intelligent mode
 l routing is becoming critical infrastructure. Choosing the right model is
  only half the challenge. Organizations also need to secure credentials\, 
 enforce governance policies\, protect sensitive data\, and maintain visibi
 lity across every AI interaction.\nJoin experts from Kong and NVIDIA to ex
 plore how Kong AI Gateway and NVIDIA NeMo Switchyard work together to make
  intelligent model routing secure\, cost-efficient\, and production-ready.
  Discover how Kong AI Gateway provides centralized security\, governance\,
  and observability across AI traffic while NeMo Switchyard dynamically sel
 ects models based on quality\, cost\, latency\, and confidence.\nSee the i
 ntegration in action through a live demonstration and explore benchmark re
 sults showing how optimized routing reduced cost per completed task while 
 maintaining task completion rates.\n**You'll leave with:**\n\n* **A framew
 ork for secure AI governance:** Discover how Kong AI Gateway centralizes c
 redentials\, enforces guardrails and PII masking\, applies rate limits\, a
 nd provides auditability across model interactions.\n* **A smarter approac
 h to model selection:** Learn how NVIDIA NeMo Switchyard dynamically route
 s agent requests across open and proprietary models\, including NVIDIA Nem
 otron\, to optimize cost and performance.\n* **Real-world performance insi
 ghts:** Explore benchmark results demonstrating how intelligent routing op
 timization reduced cost per completed task by **nearly half**\, without co
 mpromising task completion.\n* **A practical path to production-ready agen
 tic AI:** Understand how open model routing and centralized governance sup
 port secure\, scalable AI infrastructure aligned with the Open Secure AI A
 lliance's principles.
LOCATION:Online event\,
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:México City AI\, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup|Nov 
 5 - Visual AI Agriculture Meetup|Online
DTSTART:20261105T110000
CATEGORIES:ai,data,frontend,python,security
DESCRIPTION:México City AI\, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup\
 nJoin our virtual meetup to hear talks from experts on cutting-edge topics
  at the intersection of agriculture and AI.\n\n**Date\, Time and Location*
 *\n\nNov 05\, 2026\n9:00 AM - 11:00 AM PST\nOnline. **[Register for the Zo
 om!](https://voxel51.com/events/visual-ai-agriculture-meetup-november-5-20
 26)**\n\nTalks will include:\n\n**U-Net Framework for Micro-Scale Surface 
 Damage Segmentation in High-Resolution Soybean Seed Imagery**\n\nAccurate 
 detection of surface-level seed damage is critical for soybean seed qualit
 y assurance\, yet automated micro-scale damage detection in high-resolutio
 n imagery remains an open challenge due to extreme spatial variability in 
 damage scale\, severe class imbalance across damage types\, and the comput
 ational demands of processing ultra-high resolution agricultural imagery a
 t scale. This research addresses the semantic segmentation of fine-grained
  soybean seed surface defects\, such as wrinkles\, dark spots\, and genera
 l surface damage\, in 6048 × 4024 pixel images where target damages can b
 e as small as 18 × 18 pixels\, using an augmented dataset of 77\,000 indi
 vidual seed images.\n\nTo overcome the difficulties of micro-scale detecti
 on\, spatial sparsity\, and class confusion\, we propose a two-stage train
 ing and dual model inference framework built on an optimized U-Net archite
 cture with a ResNet34 encoder. In the first stage\, a damage specialist mo
 del is trained using weighted loss functions and a class-balanced approach
  that prioritizes damage classes.\n\nIn the second stage\, transfer learni
 ng is applied to initialize a healthy seed specialist model from Stage 1 w
 eights\, with rebalanced class weights and tile probabilities that identif
 y healthy seeds. During inference\, a confidence-gated damage filter suppr
 esses low-confidence predictions\, and healthy seed labels are assigned on
 ly when the specialist model's confidence exceeds that of the damage model
 .\n\nThe two specialist models achieve validation accuracies of 94% and 98
 .53%\, respectively\, and the combined inference system successfully detec
 ts and localizes all three damage categories across unseen test images und
 er conditions of extreme spatial variability and class imbalance. Qualitat
 ive evaluation confirms close alignment of predicted boundaries with groun
 d truth annotations across all damage types\, including dark spots.\n\nThe
 se results demonstrate that confidence-gated dual model inference can redu
 ce class confusion in imbalanced micro-scale segmentation\, advancing the 
 feasibility of fine-grained automated seed quality inspection at the scale
 .\n\n*About the Speaker*\n\n[Saurav Upadhyaya](https://www.linkedin.com/in
 /sauravupadhyaya/) is an AI/ML researcher with a Master's degree in Comput
 er Science\, whose work spans agricultural AI\, conversational systems\, a
 nd public health\, consistently translating advanced technology into tangi
 ble real-world impact.\n\n**From camera to drone: wildfire detection and i
 ntegration at the edge**\n\nWildfires are getting larger and more expensiv
 e every year. But caught early\, a fire is a small job for a small team\; 
 caught late\, nothing stops it. The cameras to catch them are already inst
 alled\, so the work is not necessary more sensors but making the ones we h
 ave act.\n\nThis talk walks the whole chain: a small vision model running 
 on the camera that flags smoke\, an integration layer that scores the aler
 t against terrain\, weather and history to decide whether it matters\, and
  a drone dispatched to confirm before anyone commits a crew. We will cover
  what has to run at the edge and why\, how small the model can get before 
 it stops seeing smoke\, and what it takes to trust a detection nobody has 
 looked at yet.\n\n*About the Speaker*\n\n[Maxime Carriere](https://voxel51
 .com/events/www.linkedin.com/in/maxime-carriere-871756161) is co-founder o
 f Kernwerk in Berlin\, where he works on compressing AI models to run on c
 heap embedded hardware.\n\n**5\,000 Flights to Answer One Question: Can a 
 Drone Sample as Well as a Human?**\n\nEnvironmental testing still begins w
 ith a person walking onto a site with a shovel. We built a system that tur
 ns a plain-language brief into a sampling campaign\, flies it\, and return
 s soil\, water and vegetation samples with GPS\, timestamps and chain of c
 ustody intact: 5\,000 flights\, roughly 9\,000 miles and 570 flight hours 
 over a 185-acre site in Roatan\, much of it under canopy where GPS degrade
 s and clearances are tight.\n\nI will walk through the vision and planning
  stack\, including multispectral and thermal canopy sensing\, terrain and 
 land-cover mapping\, and the constraint solver that clears a route against
  airspace and battery budget before anything leaves the ground. Then the h
 arder problem: evidentiary comparability.\n\nA drone-collected result mean
 s nothing to a regulator unless it agrees with a hand-collected split unde
 r the same method\, so I will show the dual-collection protocol we designe
 d to test exactly that. I will close on why calibrated uncertainty and kno
 wing when a model should refuse to answer matter more than raw accuracy on
 ce the output lands in a regulatory filing.\n\n*About the Speaker*\n\n[Roh
 an Talwadia](https://www.linkedin.com/in/rohantalwadia/) is co-founder and
  CTO of LabGPT\, which automates environmental field sampling using drones
  and edge analysis\, with results returned through ISO/IEC 17025-accredite
 d partner laboratories.
LOCATION:Online event\,
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AWS User Group Jalisco|Construyendo agentes de IA con Strands SDK:
  de loops simples a multi-agentes|México|Jalisco
DTSTART:20261105T190000
CATEGORIES:cloud,frontend,mobile
DESCRIPTION:AWS User Group Jalisco\nEste noviembre nos ponemos manos a la 
 obra con un workshop práctico de agentes de IA... ¡y edición especial d
 e Halloween! 🤖🎃\n\nConstruiremos paso a paso un agente de IA para se
 rvicio al cliente\, listo para producción\, usando Strands Agents\, el SD
 K de código abierto. Después lo pondremos en producción en Amazon Bedro
 ck AgentCore. El workshop tiene módulos prácticos y en cada uno le sumas
  una nueva funcionalidad a tu agente.\n\n🎤 Workshop impartido por: Axel
  Espinosa\, Associate Developer Advocate en AWS\n🏢 Además\, abriremos 
 con una charla breve de SoftServe relacionada con el tema del taller.\n
 🎃 Concurso de disfraces: ¡ven disfrazado! Habrá votación y premios p
 ara los mejores disfraces. La participación es opcional\, pero muy recome
 ndada 😉\n🍕 Habrá pizza\, bebidas y snacks de Halloween.\n\n🗓️ 
 Agenda\n\n* 7:00 PM: Bienvenida\n* 7:05 PM: “Crear un agente de IA es so
 lo el principio: conoce Amazon Bedrock AgentCore”\, con Guillermo Galvá
 n (SoftServe)\n* 7:35 PM: Workshop Strands Agents con Axel Espinosa\, prim
 era parte\n* 8:20 PM: Pausa para comer 🍕\n* 8:35 PM: Workshop\, segunda
  parte\n* 9:20 PM: Concurso de disfraces\, votación y premios 🎃\n* 9:3
 0 PM: Cierre\n\n💻 Trae tu laptop con batería cargada\, ¡vamos a const
 ruir en vivo!\n⚠️ Cupo limitado a 50 personas.\n📍 SoftServe\, Av. A
 dolfo López Mateos Nte. 2405\, Piso 21\, Guadalajara\n🗓️ Jueves 5 de
  noviembre\n🕖 7:00 PM\n\n💜 **Código de conducta**\nEn AWS User Grou
 p Jalisco todos son bienvenidos\, sin importar su experiencia\, origen o i
 dentidad. Venimos a aprender\, compartir y pasarla bien\, así que tratemo
 s a todos con respeto. No hay espacio para el acoso ni la discriminación.
  Si algo no se siente bien\, búscanos a cualquiera de los organizadores y
  lo vemos juntos.\n\nGracias a SoftServe por recibirnos y a AWS por seguir
  impulsando a la comunidad. Como siempre\, gracias por ser parte de la com
 unidad y por seguir construyendo juntos 🚀
LOCATION:SoftServe Mexico\, Av Adolfo López Mateos Nte 2405-Piso 21 int. 
 2102\, Italia Providencia\, 44648 Guadalajara\, Jal.\, Mexico
