BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:México City AI\, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup|Nov 
 9 - Agentic Labeling for Specialized Visual Data|Online
DTSTART:20261109T110000
CATEGORIES:ai,data,frontend
DESCRIPTION:México City AI\, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup\
 n**Date\, Time and Location**\n\nNov 09\, 2026\n9:00 AM - 10:00 AM PST\nOn
 line. **[Register for the Zoom!](https://voxel51.com/events/when-prompting
 -beats-training-agentic-labeling-for-specialized-visual-data-november-9-20
 26)**\n\nFrontier multimodal models handle familiar concepts well and stru
 ggle on niche ones: sorting drill-core samples into 35 geological classes\
 , or telling adhesion from scarring on a ceramic substrate. Our study acro
 ss 11 specialized visual datasets in manufacturing inspection\, geology\, 
 and medical imaging found that a few labeled examples in the prompt can cl
 ose much of that gap\, and it also found where that stops working.\n\n**Wh
 at you’ll learn:**\n\n* Niche versus hard: how in-context examples suppl
 y domain knowledge a model is missing\, and how to tell a niche task from 
 a genuinely hard one\n* What the study measured: on an industrial defect t
 ask\, one labeled example per class raised macro-F1 from 34% to 59% with n
 o fine-tuning\, while on other tasks trained specialists pulled ahead at 5
  to 10 examples per class\n* Building a few-shot labeling task: define cla
 sses\, pick reference examples\, preview predictions on a small batch\, an
 d refine the instructions\n* Finding the crossover point: when to stop pro
 mpting a foundation model and train a specialist on bootstrapped labels\n*
  Running it on your own data: attendees get free GPU compute from Nebius t
 o try the workflow after the session
LOCATION:Online event\,
END:VEVENT
